# 25. CRON

`cron` is used for scheduled tasks.

Examples:

```text
Every minute
Every hour
Every day
```

System cron configuration can be found in locations such as:

```text
/etc/crontab
/etc/cron.d/
/etc/cron.hourly/
/etc/cron.daily/
```

---

# 26. CRON PRIVILEGE ESCALATION CONCEPT

Suppose:

```text
Root runs backup.sh every minute
```

and:

```text
Normal user can modify backup.sh
```

Then:

```text
Normal User
      ↓
Modify root-executed script
      ↓
Cron executes it as root
      ↓
Potential privilege escalation
```

This is a classic exam scenario.

---

# 27. CRON ENUMERATION

Useful commands:

```bash
cat /etc/crontab
```

and:

```bash
ls -la /etc/cron.d/
```

Also inspect scheduled jobs relevant to the lab.

