# 73. ONE-LINE EXAM ANSWER

> **Linux privilege escalation is the process of obtaining higher privileges than initially authorized by exploiting weaknesses such as excessive sudo permissions, insecure SUID/SGID binaries, writable privileged files, cron misconfigurations, dangerous capabilities, vulnerable services, exposed credentials, or kernel vulnerabilities.**

